Error [E0433]: This protocol_out_of_order.Payment.Client value is thrown away
  --> protocol_out_of_order.jet:18:8
    |
 18 |     h1.Charge(500) ?? panic("charge failed")
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `run` has no return type, so it returns nothing and the value of its last line is lost
 Fix: If `run` should return it, write `-> protocol_out_of_order.Payment.Client` after its parameter list; to discard it on purpose, write `.drop("reason")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0433

Error [E0150]: `Charge` needs `Payment.Client` in state `S2`, but `h1` is in state `S1`
  --> tests/ui/protocol_out_of_order.jet:18:8
    |
 18 |     h1.Charge(500) ?? panic("charge failed")
    |        ^^^^^^
 Why: Typestate (D-STATE1): `Charge` is only valid in state `S2`; calling it in `S1` is the out-of-order-events bug it prevents
 Fix: Transition it first: call `recv_Ack` to reach `S2`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
